meta {
  name: Create Daily Log - All Fields Example
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngperson/daily-logs
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  youngperson: 4
  house: 2
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  chronology_id: 5
  activity_action: Young person participated in various activities throughout the day. Started with morning exercise, attended educational sessions, and participated in group activities in the evening.
  activity_topic: Daily Activities and Engagement
  mood[0]: Happy
  mood[1]: Excited
  mood[2]: Calm
  clothing: Casual wear - jeans and t-shirt
  breakfast: Toast with scrambled eggs, orange juice
  lunch: Chicken sandwich with salad, apple
  dinner: Pasta with vegetables, fruit salad
  snacks: Crackers and cheese, banana
  wake_up_time: 07:30
  wake_up_notes: Woke up naturally in a good mood, ready for the day
  engaged: Highly engaged in all activities
  positive_behaviour: 0
  cause_for_concern: 1
  behaviour_of_concern: 1
  attachments[0]: @file(/home/umer/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot from 2025-12-29 15-50-05.png)
  attachments[1]: @file(/home/umer/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot from 2025-12-31 16-32-45.png)
  wellbeing_category: Physical Wellbeing
  action_observation: action_observation
}

docs {
  # Create Daily Log Activity - Complete Field Reference
  
  This document shows ALL possible fields that can be sent when creating a daily log activity.
  
  ## Server Auto-Generated Fields (DO NOT SEND)
  - `date` - Auto-generated from current date
  - `log_date_time` - Auto-generated from current timestamp
  - `day_part` - Auto-detected based on current time:
    - Morning: 06:00 - 11:59
    - Afternoon: 12:00 - 17:59
    - Evening: 18:00 - 21:59
    - Night: 22:00 - 05:59
  
  ---
  
  ## REQUIRED FIELDS
  
  ### `chronology_id` (integer, required)
  - The ID of the chronology type
  - Must be global or belong to the house
  - Different chronology types require different additional fields (see below)
  
  ---
  
  ## OPTIONAL FIELDS (Common to All Chronology Types)
  
  ### Activity Information
  - **`activity_action`** (string, optional)
    - Description of the activity or action
    - Text field
    - Example: "Young person participated in football practice"
  
  - **`activity_topic`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Topic or subject of the activity
    - Example: "Sports and Recreation"
  
  ### Mood & Appearance
  - **`mood`** (array, optional)
    - Can select multiple moods
    - Options: Happy, Sad, Angry, Confused, Excited, Anxious, Calm, Frustrated, Content, Tired
    - Format: mood[0]=Happy, mood[1]=Excited
  
  - **`clothing`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Description of what the young person is wearing
    - Example: "School uniform", "Casual jeans and t-shirt"
  
  ### Meals
  - **`breakfast`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Breakfast details
    - Example: "Cereal with milk, toast, orange juice"
  
  - **`lunch`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Lunch details
    - Example: "Chicken sandwich, crisps, apple"
  
  - **`dinner`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Dinner details
    - Example: "Pasta with tomato sauce, salad, garlic bread"
  
  - **`snacks`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Snacks consumed
    - Example: "Apple, biscuits, yogurt"
  
  ### Sleep Information
  - **`wake_up_time`** (time, optional, format: HH:MM)
    - Time the young person woke up
    - Example: "07:30", "08:15"
  
  - **`wake_up_notes`** (string, optional)
    - Notes about waking up
    - Example: "Woke up naturally in a good mood"
  
  ### Behaviour Tracking
  - **`engaged`** (string, optional, max 191 chars)
    - Level or description of engagement
    - Example: "Highly engaged", "Partially engaged", "Disengaged"
  
  - **`positive_behaviour`** (boolean, optional)
    - Whether positive behaviour was observed
    - Values: true, false, 1, 0
    - Default: false
  
  - **`cause_for_concern`** (boolean, optional)
    - Whether there is a cause for concern
    - Values: true, false, 1, 0
    - Default: false
  
  - **`behaviour_of_concern`** (boolean, optional)
    - Whether concerning behaviour was noted
    - Values: true, false, 1, 0
    - Default: false
  
  ### Attachments
  - **`attachments`** (array of files, optional)
    - Supported formats: PDF, JPG, JPEG, PNG, DOC, DOCX
    - Maximum size: 10MB per file
    - Returns with `full_url` field containing temporary signed URL
    - Format: attachments[0]=@file(...), attachments[1]=@file(...)
  
  ---
  
  ## CHRONOLOGY-SPECIFIC REQUIRED FIELDS
  
  ### For "Health & Wellbeing" (chronology_id = 4)
  - **`wellbeing_category`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Options: "Physical Wellbeing", "Emotional wellbeing", "Mental wellbeing", "Sleep and Rest"
  
  - **`action_observation`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Detailed observation or action taken
    - Example: "Young person participated in sports activities. Showed good stamina."
  
  ### For "Views, Wishes and Feelings" (chronology_id = 5)
  - **`entry_type`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Options: "View", "Wish", "Feeling", "Concern", "Complaint", "Compliment"
  
  - **`action_observation`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Details of the view/wish/feeling
    - Example: "YP expressed wish to visit family more frequently"
  
  ### For "Protection, Behaviour and Safeguarding" (chronology_id = 6)
  - **`safeguarding_category`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Options: "Physical", "Emotional", "Sexual", "Neglect", "Bullying", "Online Safety", "Exploitation"
  
  - **`concern_raised`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Description of the safeguarding concern
    - Example: "YP disclosed concerns about online interactions"
  
  - **`disclosure_made`** (string, optional)
    - Details of any disclosure made
  
  - **`action_outcome`** (string, optional)
    - Outcome of actions taken
  
  - **`review_date`** (date, optional, must be today or future)
    - Date scheduled for review
    - Format: YYYY-MM-DD
    - Example: "2026-02-15"
  
  - **`follow_up`** (string, optional)
    - Follow-up actions needed
  
  ### For "Behaviour Monitor Chart" OR "Enjoy & Achieve" (chronology_id = 2 or 3)
  - **`action_observation`** (string, REQUIRED)
    - Detailed behaviour observation or achievement details
    - Example: "YP showed excellent cooperation during group activities"
  
  ---
  
  ## RESPONSE EXAMPLE (201 Created)
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Daily log activity created successfully",
    "data": {
      "id": 123,
      "yp_daily_log_id": 45,
      "day_part": "Afternoon",
      "log_date_time": "2026-01-27T14:30:15.000000Z",
      "chronology_id": 1,
      "activity_action": "Young person participated in various activities...",
      "activity_topic": "Daily Activities and Engagement",
      "mood": ["Happy", "Excited", "Calm"],
      "clothing": "Casual wear - jeans and t-shirt",
      "breakfast": "Toast with scrambled eggs, orange juice",
      "lunch": "Chicken sandwich with salad, apple",
      "dinner": "Pasta with vegetables, fruit salad",
      "snacks": "Crackers and cheese, banana",
      "wake_up_time": "07:30",
      "wake_up_notes": "Woke up naturally in a good mood",
      "engaged": "Highly engaged in all activities",
      "positive_behaviour": true,
      "cause_for_concern": false,
      "behaviour_of_concern": false,
      "attachments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "original_name": "daily_activity_photo.jpg",
          "filename": "abc123.jpg",
          "path": "daily_logs/yp_4/abc123.jpg",
          "full_url": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucket/daily_logs/yp_4/abc123.jpg?signature=...",
          "size": 245680,
          "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
          "created_at": "2026-01-27T14:30:15.000000Z"
        }
      ],
      "created_by": 42,
      "created_at": "2026-01-27T14:30:15.000000Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-27T14:30:15.000000Z"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ## VALIDATION ERRORS EXAMPLE
  
  If required chronology-specific fields are missing:
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "message": "Validation failed",
    "errors": {
      "chronology_id": ["Please select a chronology."],
      "wellbeing_category": ["Well-being category is required for Health & Wellbeing logs."],
      "action_observation": ["Action/Observation is required for this chronology type."]
    },
    "available_options": {
      "available_chronologies": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "No Activity",
          "is_global": true,
          "belongs_to_house": false
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "name": "Health & Wellbeing",
          "is_global": true,
          "belongs_to_house": false
        }
      ],
      "mood": ["Happy", "Sad", "Angry", "Confused", "Excited", "Anxious", "Calm", "Frustrated", "Content", "Tired"]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ## IMPORTANT NOTES
  
  1. **Auto-Generated Fields**: Do NOT send `date`, `log_date_time`, or `day_part` - they are automatically generated by the server
  
  2. **Parent Daily Log**: If no daily log exists for the current date, it will be created automatically
  
  3. **Multiple Activities**: You can create multiple activities for the same day - they will all be linked to the same daily log
  
  4. **Attachments**: Stored in cloud storage (S3) and return temporary signed URLs valid for limited time
  
  5. **Chronology Validation**: The required fields depend on the chronology type selected
  
  6. **Boolean Fields**: Can send as true/false or 1/0
  
  7. **Mood Array**: Can send multiple mood values using array notation
  
  8. **File Size Limits**: Each attachment must be under 10MB
  
  9. **Character Limits**: Most string fields have a 191 character limit (except text fields like activity_action, wake_up_notes)
  
  10. **Time Format**: wake_up_time must be in 24-hour format (HH:MM) like "07:30" or "14:45"
}
